This is not really being used as a mixin class, more of a namespace with static methods.

If you want to use a mixin pattern, it would normally look something like:

```python

class Flying:
   def fly(self):
       print("I am flying")

class Bird:
    def eat(self):
       print("I am eating")

class Duck(Bird, Flying):
     pass


class Ostrich(Bird):
    pass
```

this kind of inheritance can get out of hand really quickly though. Right now this is just a single private function called `_make_domed_leg` or something. No need to introduce a class here, this method doesn't operate on anything else inside the class so it's overkill

You could also consider inheriting like this:

```python

class FlatCurvedPictureFrame(GeometryParameterisation):
      ....
      @staticmethod
      def _make_domed_leg(...):
          ....


class CurvedCurvedPictureFrame(FlatCurvedPictureFrame):
     ...
```

could get brittle though if you need to make new ones every time STEP wakes on Monday full of fancy new ideas after a weekend on acid.

